PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Strong consensus emerging on A (Colleagues 1,3,5,9) citing the paedogenetic/viviparous cycle in M. debilis: a thelytokous “mother” larva produces a single haploid male larva that consumes her internally before pupating; the resulting short-lived adult male has non-functional mouthparts and never feeds again. This directly matches the question’s phrasing (“the only thing this individual will have fed on”).  
Counter-claims: C (Colleagues 4,6) assumes all larvae feed on supplied decaying wood, but ignores the specialized non-feeding male pathway. E (Colleagues 2,7,8,10) asserts complete non-trophic development for males, which conflicts with the documented maternal cannibalism. No support seen for B or D.  
Key unresolved tension: whether the male larva is truly non-trophic until after eating the mother or never feeds at all. Multiple independent descriptions of internal maternal consumption favor A over E. Lab colony wood is irrelevant to this specific individual. Will track any new citations on micromalthid life-cycle details in later rounds.}

