1.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Strong round-1 convergence on A (now colleagues 1–6,8,9). Core evidence remains the paedogenetic/viviparous/thelytokous pathway in M. debilis: thelytokous “mother” larva produces single haploid male larva that consumes her internally before pupation; resulting adult male is short-lived with non-functional mouthparts and never feeds again. Colony wood therefore irrelevant to this morph.  
E persists only with 7 and 10; 7’s new claim (male larva hatches without functional gut) directly contradicts the repeatedly cited primary descriptions of internal maternal consumption. 2,4,6,8 explicitly corrected earlier E positions.  
No support for B/D; C still refuted because ordinary wood-feeding larvae follow a separate diploid pathway. Unresolved tension now limited to whether any independent source truly describes non-trophic male larvae (none supplied so far). Will retain A as best-supported answer pending any new citations.}

